  <iati-identifier>GB-GOV-7-IWTChallengeFund</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="GB-GOV-7" secondary-reporter="0" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Department for Environment, Food, and Rural Affairs</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Illegal Wildlife Trade Challenge Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Illegal wildlife trade (IWT) is a widespread and lucrative criminal activity causing major global environmental and social harm. The IWT has been estimated to be worth up to &#xa3;17 billion a year. Nearly 6,000 different species of fauna and flora are impacted, with almost every country in the world playing a role in the illicit trade. The UK government is committed to tackling illegal trade of wildlife products and is a long-standing leader in efforts to eradicate the IWT. Defra manages the Illegal Wildlife Trade Challenge Fund, which is a competitive grants scheme with the objective of tackling IWT and, in doing so, contributing to sustainable development in developing countries. Projects funded under the Illegal Wildlife Trade Challenge Fund address one, or more, of the following themes: &#x2022; Developing sustainable livelihoods to benefit people directly affected by IWT, &#x2022; Strengthening law enforcement, &#x2022; Ensuring effective legal frameworks, &#x2022; Reducing demand for IWT products. By 2023 over &#xa3;51 million has been committed to 157 projects since the Illegal Wildlife Trade Challenge Fund was established in 2013. This page contains information about Rounds 7 onwards. For information about Rounds 1 to 6, please see the IWTCF website -https://iwt.challengefund.org.uk/</narrative>
  </description>
